_medica","section":"rectum","label":"Rectum","startLine":9538,"endLine":9538,"text":"Diarrhoea ; bearing down in abdomen and"},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"urinary","label":"Urine","startLine":9541,"endLine":9555,"text":"Green; frothy; contains bile, sugar.\n\nRelationship, — Compare: Tinospora cordifolia (a\nHindoo medicine for chronic cases of fever with en-\nlarged spleen). Polymnia uvedalia (acute splenitis\nwith tenderness over left hypochondriac region; spleen\nenlarged, ague cake. Vascular atony, tissues sodden,\nflabby and non-elastic. Enlarged glands; influences all\nductless glands.)\n\n214\n\n\nCompare : Berberis; Myrica; Cedron."},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"modalities","label":"Modalities","startLine":9556,"endLine":9557,"text":"Worse, motion, lying on left side."}],"corpusPassages":[]}